WEBVTT

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:16.990
<b>Original Story, Screenplay, and Mechanics Design</b>

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:16.990
<b>KATSUHIRO OTOMO</b>

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:28.000
Haruko!

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.010
<b>Original Character Design</b>

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.010
<b>HISASHI EGUCHI</b>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:43.350
Haruko, I wet my bed.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:44.020
<b>Animation Director</b>

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:44.020
<b>FUMIO IIDA</b>

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:53.860
I feel awful, Haruko.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:58.030
Haruko.

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.040
<b>Art Director</b>

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:02.040
<b>HIROSHI SASAKI</b>

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.040
Just a decade
after its creation...

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.380
the Medical Crisis Network
is already overloaded.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:13.460
We distribute Medical Alert
pendants to the chronically ill...

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.050
such as heart patients
and the elderly.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:18.720
We've given out
7 million pendants!

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:23.060
The nursing homes are
filled to capacity...

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:23.060
<b>Director of Photography</b>

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:23.060
<b>NHIDEO OKAZAKI</b>

00:01:23.060 --> 00:01:25.600
and they can't
afford modern equipment.

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:30.360
We're also experiencing
shortages of in-home staff.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.650
There aren't enough nurses, and
their salaries are skyrocketing.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.150
Excuse me.

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:45.160
I have a solution to all
the problems of the elderly!

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.160
<b>Music
BUN ITAKURA</b>

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:46.160
<b>Theme Song
MISHIO OGAWA</b>

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:48.670
This will
revolutionise medicine!

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.840
I have a blueprint for a new
society, respecting the elderly.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.760
Within a single decade, we can
eliminate all of our problems...

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.640
and grant the elderly
a rich, full life!

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:06.930
And to cap this magnificent
dream, we already have funding!

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.270
The Ministry of
Public Welfare...

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:13.190
has been given the greatest
project of this century!

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:15.190
This is our task.

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:19.700
I present you with the most
important work of our era...

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:23.490
a project that will
reconcile the young and old...

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:25.700
and the answer to every
problem of the elderly!

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.080
The solution is...

00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:31.210
Here!

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.210
<b>Chief Director</b>

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:35.210
<b>HIROYUKI KITAKUBO</b>

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:44.720
<b>ROU</b>

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.390
<b>JIN</b>

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.230
<b>Z</b>

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:15.250
<b>ROUJIN Z</b>

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:15.250
<b>Calligraphy by
KATSUHIRO OTOMO</b>

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.760
This fight is one-sided!

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.690
You can't do that,
Mr. Takazawa.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:39.530
You can't use the alert pendant
just because you wet yourself.

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.030
Dr. Misaka was
really upset...

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:47.540
when you pushed it in the
middle of the night last week.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.380
Get off him!

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:06.970
You're only supposed to use
the pendant in an emergency!

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.730
That sounds close.

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:28.240
I'm coming!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:31.830
Coming!

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.500
I...

00:04:39.130 --> 00:04:40.550
This is the man.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:43.300
Mr. Takazawa!
You pushed it again!

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.680
Who are you?

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.970
I'm Haruko Mihashi,
a student nurse.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:49.810
I'm his volunteer nurse.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.430
He used his pendant
again, didn't he?

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:54.100
I keep telling him.

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:56.100
Mr. Kijuro Takazawa...

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.060
you're coming with us.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.070
What's going on?

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.650
He's going to assist us.

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.660
We're with the Ministry
of Public Welfare.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.580
Ministry of
Public Welfare?

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.910
His family has
granted permission.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.210
Haruko!

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:15.410
Mr. Takazawa!

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:24.550
Excuse me, but where
are you taking him?

00:05:24.550 --> 00:05:31.220
<i>Haru Takazawa</i>

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:44.320
...and that's how the body
absorbs the nutrients from food.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:48.660
This entire process
takes about 24 hours.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:51.780
Then the food is
excreted as waste.

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:57.500
Next week, we'll
pick up with the anus.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:06.840
Haruko!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.010
I finally got
tickets to Ink Stick!

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:11.720
Let's go!

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:12.430
Did you hear?

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.930
What?

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:19.560
Dr. Tachibana got a letter from
the Ministry of Public Welfare.

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.810
The Ministry?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:24.940
They've made a breakthrough
in nursing equipment.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.700
They're going to test
it on Kijuro Takazawa!

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:33.240
This band is hot! Their
concert will be recorded live!

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:36.080
What kind of
nursing equipment?

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.330
I don't know.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:42.920
The press conference is at three
today in the welfare centre.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.090
Three o'clock?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:46.920
It's nearly three now!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:09.610
Our society is being crushed
under a growing problem.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:11.610
The problem of the elderly.

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:17.580
How far are we willing to go
to preserve our nation's elders?

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:21.750
Everywhere we turn, there are
painful choices to be made.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:24.340
But now an answer screams out:

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:28.090
The Z-001!

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:33.720
It's a priceless addition
to any hospital...

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:39.600
yet this new invention will
prove most useful in the home.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.020
See for yourselves.

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:56.700
An ultrasonic bath will clean
every pore of the patient's body!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:04.750
The bathing schedule
can be pre-programmed.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.090
The bed senses humidity
and perspiration...

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:12.050
and will adjust the temperature
and frequency of baths.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:20.180
Excretion!

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:25.650
An elderly person's most
embarrassing problem!

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:29.270
This problem terrifies even
the most devoted family.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:32.240
But our machine has
eliminated the problem!

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.820
If the system
detects a faint odour...

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:40.490
an extension automatically
vacuums waste from the patient.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:45.540
The crisis is over before an
invalid can call for assistance.

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:49.500
Dignity is maintained.
No mess, no embarrassment.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:54.680
The bedridden often have
a surplus of leisure time.

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:58.140
So naturally, our machine
provides ample entertainment.

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:03.270
The bed includes hi-fi stereo,
radio, TV, and phone modules.

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.640
Patients can buy
or sell stock.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:08.560
They can watch races
or follow sports.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.190
They can even go shopping
around the world!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:16.200
There are programs for chess,
Go, Othello, and video games.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:19.660
A word processor helps
write haiku and poetry.

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:24.460
A patient can even call up his
friends in their own Z-001 beds.

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:28.500
A patient can talk with up to
four friends simultaneously!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:33.710
And if there are no friends, just
input an image and personality.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:36.760
The computer will provide a
simulated conversation partner.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:42.810
But there's more!
A built-in feeding station!

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:53.440
The Z-001 holds food for
a week including dessert.

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:59.070
Patients can download
their favourite recipes.

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:07.410
And after eating, what could be
better than a little exercise?

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.830
All without leaving the
comfort of your own bed.

00:10:13.550 --> 00:10:16.260
It's important to stretch first,
especially the back.

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:19.340
Patients can walk or row.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:24.100
They can even swim
in the bath water.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:37.240
But that's not all. The Z-001 is a
perfect analysis station.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:45.200
It monitors blood pressure,
breathing, heart rate, and EEG.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.040
And if any of these vital signs
should become abnormal...

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:52.920
the computer can provide
an instant diagnosis.

00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:56.130
If a medical history
has been input...

00:10:56.130 --> 00:11:01.510
the bed can even prescribe a
treatment such as oxygen.

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:04.600
Or if the situation
is more serious...

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.520
the bed will connect
to the local data net.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:10.560
The bed can send out a call...

00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:13.980
alerting the family doctor,
hospital, or other institutions.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.320
It can even
handle disasters...

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:25.830
such as an earthquake,
typhoon, or robbery!

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.910
But that means...!

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:33.790
Exactly!
A sixth-generation computer!

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:39.210
It has self-enhancement
capabilities.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:43.510
It exceeds the learning abilities
of fifth-generation systems.

00:11:43.510 --> 00:11:46.100
It can even upgrade
its own hardware.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.430
It is truly a dream computer.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.940
Excuse me!
What powers it?

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:56.860
Nuclear power!
A miniature atomic furnace!

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:59.940
What if there's a radiation leak?

00:11:59.940 --> 00:12:05.740
Don't worry, there's a built-in
super-sensitive alarm.

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.830
It's completely safe.

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:10.000
It really <i>is</i> safe,
isn't it!

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.790
Wait a minute!

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.670
I'm sure it's a
wonderful machine...

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:19.500
but look at Mr. Takazawa
just lying there.

00:12:20.460 --> 00:12:22.590
I feel sorry for him.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:27.470
How can a machine give him
the love he needs?

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:30.220
I remember you.

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:33.480
I'm Mr. Takazawa's...

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:37.480
You're right! Nothing can
replace the love of a family.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:40.650
But we can help that family
as much as possible.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:44.570
We want to give the
elderly a rich, full life!

00:12:44.570 --> 00:12:46.910
That is our dream.

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:52.250
Which is why we at the
Ministry of Public Welfare...

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:55.040
lovingly present
the Z-001!

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:02.170
Terada!

00:13:04.050 --> 00:13:05.380
Huh? What?

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.180
The Secretary of Public
Welfare is here!

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:57.640
Geriatrics has sure
come a long way.

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:00.940
But they shouldn't
dump people in machines.

00:14:00.940 --> 00:14:03.400
That just hides the problem.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.490
Yeah, it doesn't feel right.

00:14:07.450 --> 00:14:13.200
But we shouldn't have to devote
our whole lives to old people.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:15.580
The geezers probably agree.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.580
You're so selfish!

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:21.250
Life is more than
just lying in bed.

00:14:21.250 --> 00:14:23.000
Haruko!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.550
How did the
announcement go?

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:29.680
Stop it! The experimental
subject was Haruko's patient.

00:14:29.680 --> 00:14:32.550
That must have been a shock.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:42.360
On my computer?

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.990
I thought
you'd left it turned on.

00:14:55.370 --> 00:14:57.370
But it's on every channel.

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:09.220
It's a message from someone,
but what a way to send it!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:11.930
I guess you got the
message, right?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:14.260
You're giving me the creeps.

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:19.180
I have to get a print-out!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.890
I'll get a cable.

00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:22.190
How come?

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:23.610
Just gathering evidence.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.760
Tomoe?

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.800
What's going on here?

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.900
What happened?
Are they broken?

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:12.150
I didn't do it!

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.780
Don't be so defensive!

00:16:16.700 --> 00:16:18.030
Mr. Takazawa!

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:25.670
<b>Help me, Haruko
Help me, Haruko</b>

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.960
Maybe you're right,
but still...

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:34.590
Let's think about this before
we get too carried away.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:38.390
What a worm!
You're just scared.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:44.190
Right. We got an SOS,
so we're coming to help.

00:16:58.330 --> 00:17:00.040
I need a light here!

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.160
Okay.

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:08.670
Figured it out?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.170
Are you kidding?
Look at this thing!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:17.590
Come on, let's go.
What if we get caught?

00:17:17.590 --> 00:17:21.180
You are so spineless!

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:23.770
What's the big deal?

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:26.650
He's just an old man!

00:17:27.520 --> 00:17:29.190
I can't abandon him!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:33.190
After all,
we have a solemn duty...

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:36.200
as nursing volunteers!

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.410
Haruko, was it?

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.460
What are you doing here?

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:53.420
This is a government facility.
It's closed to the public.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.550
Mr. Takazawa was
calling for help.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:57.680
Calling for help?

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:02.470
He sent a message to
my computer this afternoon.

00:18:07.270 --> 00:18:08.560
Get out of there.

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:19.410
There <i>is</i> evidence of a
message being transmitted.

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:23.120
Thank you!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:27.000
Now that you've informed us,
we can solve the problem!

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:29.920
Excellent work!

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:31.670
Really?

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:34.250
Haruko, that's great!

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:39.630
Thank God! I was afraid
we'd be arrested!

00:18:39.630 --> 00:18:41.340
But what about
Mr. Takazawa?

00:18:41.340 --> 00:18:43.680
He'll be fine now.
Hasegawa!

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:46.310
I'll call the
supervising physician.

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:48.730
Hasegawa here...

00:18:48.730 --> 00:18:51.310
Haruko,
let's go home.

00:18:51.310 --> 00:18:53.020
Satisfied?

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:54.770
They'll take care of it.

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:58.950
This will take a while, so
you might as well go home.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:01.410
I'll see you to the door.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:05.580
Yes, that's right.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:10.500
Haruko...

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.460
Help me!

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.090
What's going on?

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.720
But I turned off the
autonomous calculation circuits.

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:21.590
Mr. Takazawa!

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:25.680
You fool!

00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.720
Haruko!

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:30.060
Mr. Takazawa is
calling for help!

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.390
You can't do that!

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:36.820
Probes are wired into his
trachea and nervous system.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.070
Pulling it off
could kill him!

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:40.900
That's terrible!

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.910
We have his
family's permission.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:47.290
Do you have
<i>his</i> permission?

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.580
I'll call the project leader.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.330
Fiend!

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:51.040
Monster!

00:19:51.040 --> 00:19:52.210
Elder abuse!

00:19:52.210 --> 00:19:54.290
Let him go!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:20:00.010
Get out of here!
You kids don't know anything!

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:08.680
Yes, send the police, please.

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:14.230
Mr. Terada!

00:20:17.360 --> 00:20:21.070
Haruko.

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:23.240
Let's go home.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:25.780
Yes, let's go home.

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.540
Stop!

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:39.300
Mr. Terada!

00:20:47.100 --> 00:20:49.010
It won't fit!

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.690
You idiots!

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:03.820
That bed is too big for
anything but a freight elevator.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:09.450
Let's go.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:23.090
Hey, wait!
Open up! Haruko!

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:30.220
Did you see that?

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:40.190
What are we going
to do with him?

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:43.610
We have to get this
story to the media!

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:49.410
Haru, let's go home.

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:53.500
Yes, this is Terada.
Give me Secretary Minagawa.

00:21:54.000 --> 00:21:58.250
I'm sorry to disturb you
in the middle of the night...

00:22:09.430 --> 00:22:12.140
Haruko, the bed's coming up...

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:18.190
Quiet!

00:22:22.360 --> 00:22:24.030
I'm home.

00:22:24.030 --> 00:22:25.240
Mr. Takazawa!

00:22:25.240 --> 00:22:29.860
We can't stay. I just came
to get your wife's picture.

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:35.080
The police!

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:40.330
What's going on?

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:41.080
Out of the way!

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:47.340
That rat!

00:22:48.930 --> 00:22:50.390
That guy's here too.

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:51.890
Terada?

00:22:53.560 --> 00:22:57.310
They're going to arrest us!

00:22:57.310 --> 00:23:00.730
Maybe they'll go easy on us
if we surrender!

00:23:00.730 --> 00:23:02.310
Do you see any TV crews?

00:23:02.730 --> 00:23:05.650
TV? My mother will find out!

00:23:05.650 --> 00:23:09.400
I have to tell them about the
bed before we're arrested!

00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:20.790
Stop it!

00:23:21.370 --> 00:23:24.630
I need to show
the TV crews...

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:27.090
What are you going
to tell them?

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:29.880
Were you going to give out
your friends' names?

00:23:29.880 --> 00:23:33.140
No, really!
I'm not with them!

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:34.800
Ouch!

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:34.800
<i>Stop pushing!</i>

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:36.310
Mr. Takazawa!

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:43.310
Hasegawa!

00:23:50.320 --> 00:23:51.610
Get up.

00:24:10.840 --> 00:24:14.140
I can't begin to express
how disappointed I am.

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:17.350
We were all so proud
of this project.

00:24:17.350 --> 00:24:22.310
I expect you to take full
responsibility for this, Terada.

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:23.850
I'm sorry.

00:24:23.850 --> 00:24:29.530
But there was more to this than
merely inputting faulty data.

00:24:31.240 --> 00:24:36.490
Where in the blueprints does
it mention a transforming bed?

00:24:36.490 --> 00:24:40.540
That was a feature
in case of natural disaster.

00:24:40.910 --> 00:24:46.040
We weren't properly informed
about this new computer.

00:24:47.880 --> 00:24:50.380
Where has the
black box gone?

00:24:50.380 --> 00:24:55.300
Where did we get the money
for a sixth-generation computer?

00:24:55.300 --> 00:24:59.350
The computer was donated by
the Nishibashi Corporation.

00:24:59.350 --> 00:25:05.440
How can we evaluate a machine
that we don't even understand?

00:25:07.310 --> 00:25:12.150
We never received complete
readings from the computer.

00:25:14.530 --> 00:25:17.410
Is that true?
Hasegawa?

00:25:18.740 --> 00:25:19.910
Hasegawa!

00:25:22.580 --> 00:25:23.750
Damn it!

00:25:24.120 --> 00:25:26.460
Don't mess with the
Ministry of Public Welfare!

00:25:27.290 --> 00:25:29.670
Can I use your phone?

00:25:30.590 --> 00:25:33.420
This is Hasegawa.
Yeah.

00:25:35.470 --> 00:25:37.180
Just a second.

00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:43.930
This is Minagawa.

00:25:43.930 --> 00:25:46.890
Yeah. This is Minagawa.
What?

00:25:49.150 --> 00:25:53.740
Yes, sir! Not at all.
No, sir.

00:25:53.740 --> 00:25:57.700
I'm sorry, sir.
I didn't know.

00:26:38.150 --> 00:26:40.070
Honey!

00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:48.960
Haru...

00:26:53.960 --> 00:26:57.050
For now, you'll do
all your work here in the ward.

00:26:58.050 --> 00:27:01.680
You're getting off
very lightly.

00:27:01.680 --> 00:27:02.720
Yes, sir.

00:27:04.140 --> 00:27:06.350
Well, you have work to do.

00:27:06.350 --> 00:27:07.730
Yes, sir.

00:27:20.110 --> 00:27:21.910
Three whole hours!

00:27:22.370 --> 00:27:25.870
The prof yelled at us
for three whole hours!

00:27:26.080 --> 00:27:29.870
It was terrible.
He kept blaming us!

00:27:30.250 --> 00:27:35.290
At least it's over. No one
got expelled or arrested.

00:27:35.290 --> 00:27:38.380
Let's just forget about it.

00:27:39.590 --> 00:27:44.390
Haruko, are you still
worried about him?

00:27:44.850 --> 00:27:47.810
There's nothing else
we can do.

00:27:47.810 --> 00:27:50.390
I hope this doesn't
appear in our grades.

00:27:51.190 --> 00:27:57.360
We got an SOS, and
we did everything we could.

00:27:57.360 --> 00:28:00.820
They promised to fix the bed.

00:28:00.820 --> 00:28:04.530
Besides, there's plenty of other
old men who look just like him.

00:28:04.530 --> 00:28:09.120
It's just that
he's always been my patient...

00:28:09.120 --> 00:28:11.250
since I first volunteered.

00:28:11.250 --> 00:28:12.460
You're too attached to him.

00:28:12.460 --> 00:28:13.920
Hey, you!

00:28:14.420 --> 00:28:16.590
No talking in the halls!

00:28:16.880 --> 00:28:18.090
Yeah, yeah.

00:28:18.090 --> 00:28:20.210
I still have work to do.

00:28:20.210 --> 00:28:22.340
Aren't you coming
to the bar with us?

00:28:22.340 --> 00:28:25.260
We'll be at the
Western Family.

00:28:25.260 --> 00:28:28.600
See you there!

00:28:58.340 --> 00:29:01.510
All right!
I'm in!

00:29:06.300 --> 00:29:09.760
What a stupid password!

00:29:09.760 --> 00:29:15.020
With my ALGOL program, it was
like taking candy from a baby.

00:29:17.650 --> 00:29:20.360
Hey, miss!
Did you see that?

00:29:20.360 --> 00:29:21.320
Is it a game?

00:29:21.650 --> 00:29:25.570
I just broke into the Tyrell
Corporation in America.

00:29:25.570 --> 00:29:28.530
I found evidence
of tax evasion.

00:29:30.370 --> 00:29:32.330
Tax evasion?

00:29:32.540 --> 00:29:37.960
We're going to anonymously
send this data to a newspaper.

00:29:37.960 --> 00:29:40.920
Of course,
it's legally inadmissible.

00:29:40.920 --> 00:29:44.340
Still, I bet the papers
will be interested in it.

00:29:45.220 --> 00:29:50.260
Cracking a system
is such a rush!

00:29:50.260 --> 00:29:54.770
My stiff neck is gone, and
I've got a massive hard-on!

00:29:54.770 --> 00:29:57.940
You old pervert!

00:29:59.650 --> 00:30:02.940
Are you serious?

00:30:03.650 --> 00:30:07.860
You bet I am!
Wanna see?

00:30:08.450 --> 00:30:10.570
No, not that!

00:30:10.570 --> 00:30:13.490
I'm talking about
the computer!

00:30:13.490 --> 00:30:18.620
Are you calling
me a liar?

00:30:18.620 --> 00:30:20.330
Then it <i>is</i> true?

00:30:20.710 --> 00:30:25.720
Of course. I'm the best
hacker this side of Hakone.

00:30:25.720 --> 00:30:28.630
That's because
you can't go outside.

00:30:30.680 --> 00:30:33.430
I have a huge
favour to ask you.

00:30:37.310 --> 00:30:39.230
On to the next bar!

00:30:39.230 --> 00:30:42.230
<b><i>Western Family</i></b>

00:30:42.940 --> 00:30:44.570
Here are your drinks.

00:30:44.570 --> 00:30:46.030
Coming right up!

00:30:46.030 --> 00:30:47.360
Waiter!

00:30:51.740 --> 00:30:57.750
Why does she keep talking
about that stupid old man?

00:30:58.870 --> 00:31:02.290
She dumped you,
didn't she?

00:31:03.290 --> 00:31:04.500
Shut up.

00:31:08.010 --> 00:31:10.470
Haruko's grandma...

00:31:10.470 --> 00:31:12.390
<i>You're</i> the grandma!

00:31:12.390 --> 00:31:16.810
In eighth grade, Haruko's
parents gave her a study room.

00:31:16.810 --> 00:31:20.100
They gave Haruko
her grandmother's old room.

00:31:20.480 --> 00:31:24.940
Haruko was thrilled
to get the room.

00:31:24.940 --> 00:31:26.730
But then
her grandma died...

00:31:27.730 --> 00:31:29.780
alone and unloved
in a rest home.

00:31:31.360 --> 00:31:33.620
Hey, you guys!

00:31:33.620 --> 00:31:36.620
No more sob stories!

00:31:36.950 --> 00:31:38.580
Go sing!

00:31:38.580 --> 00:31:40.120
Are you okay?

00:31:40.120 --> 00:31:41.710
Come on, Nobuko!

00:31:41.710 --> 00:31:43.630
Come on, Nobuko, try it!

00:31:44.080 --> 00:31:47.050
I guess I have to.

00:31:52.010 --> 00:31:55.640
Waiter! I want some
mackerel and a beer!

00:31:55.640 --> 00:31:57.220
Right away!

00:31:57.220 --> 00:32:00.930
The world is
such a lonely place.

00:32:00.930 --> 00:32:05.610
Why are you so gloomy,
Maeda?

00:32:28.420 --> 00:32:30.260
This is tough.

00:32:34.890 --> 00:32:37.640
All right, a challenge!

00:32:37.640 --> 00:32:41.520
Let me help.

00:32:43.230 --> 00:32:48.110
Okay. It would speed things up
if we work in parallel.

00:32:48.110 --> 00:32:52.740
Thank you. I'm really
worried about Mr. Takazawa.

00:32:52.740 --> 00:32:56.820
If I could just talk to him,
I could find out if he's okay.

00:32:56.820 --> 00:33:00.580
You must be keen to
meet this old geezer!

00:33:00.580 --> 00:33:05.000
You old fool! I'm not doing it
for that rotting old carcass!

00:33:05.000 --> 00:33:09.130
I knew it! You want
the <i>girl</i>, you pervert!

00:33:09.130 --> 00:33:15.680
I want to see what a sixth-
generation computer looks like.

00:33:44.410 --> 00:33:45.830
I did it.

00:33:45.830 --> 00:33:47.370
Really?

00:33:52.300 --> 00:33:53.760
But...

00:33:53.760 --> 00:33:55.010
What is it?

00:33:55.590 --> 00:34:00.050
I'm sending signals,
but there's no response.

00:34:00.050 --> 00:34:01.720
Sounds dead.

00:34:02.470 --> 00:34:04.770
The computer!

00:34:05.270 --> 00:34:09.350
Our data should
be getting through.

00:34:09.810 --> 00:34:12.400
Maybe we're locked out.

00:34:14.360 --> 00:34:19.990
This young lady says
she knows the guy.

00:34:19.990 --> 00:34:22.740
Try calling him.

00:34:23.410 --> 00:34:25.080
What's his name?

00:34:40.470 --> 00:34:46.560
TA

00:34:42.140 --> 00:34:46.560
KA

00:34:43.720 --> 00:34:46.560
ZA

00:34:45.350 --> 00:34:46.560
WA

00:34:47.180 --> 00:34:49.940
Wa

00:34:47.600 --> 00:34:49.940
ke

00:34:48.060 --> 00:34:49.940
up!

00:34:48.690 --> 00:34:49.940
I

00:34:48.890 --> 00:34:49.940
di

00:34:49.310 --> 00:34:49.940
ot!!

00:34:54.020 --> 00:34:56.360
It's no use.

00:34:56.360 --> 00:35:00.910
There must be a password.
We'll have to find it.

00:35:03.410 --> 00:35:04.870
Maybe...

00:35:04.870 --> 00:35:05.830
What?

00:35:41.030 --> 00:35:43.910
Could you duplicate
this person's voice?

00:35:55.500 --> 00:36:01.220
Mr. Takazawa...

00:36:04.930 --> 00:36:05.970
Mr. Takazawa...

00:36:11.310 --> 00:36:14.770
<b><i>DO NOT ENTER</i></b>

00:36:21.820 --> 00:36:24.950
Are you in pain?

00:36:25.700 --> 00:36:30.160
It's you!
You came for me!

00:36:30.160 --> 00:36:32.830
Of course.

00:36:33.460 --> 00:36:36.590
Who is it? Who's there?
This area's restricted!

00:36:37.000 --> 00:36:42.090
Are you all right?
Are you in pain?

00:36:43.050 --> 00:36:46.220
It hurts!

00:36:46.220 --> 00:36:49.390
Help me!

00:36:49.390 --> 00:36:53.270
You poor, poor man.

00:36:53.270 --> 00:36:56.610
They've been so cruel to you!

00:36:57.810 --> 00:37:00.320
Somebody help!

00:37:04.820 --> 00:37:09.370
Just hold on.
I'm going to help you.

00:37:10.910 --> 00:37:12.620
He's in pain.

00:37:13.000 --> 00:37:15.710
We have to save him.

00:37:17.170 --> 00:37:22.090
Learn anything about the
sixth-generation computer?

00:37:22.550 --> 00:37:24.300
This is incredible!

00:37:24.550 --> 00:37:29.930
Yeah. I've seen three-
dimensional architecture before.

00:37:29.930 --> 00:37:36.690
But there's something completely
unique down at the core.

00:37:36.690 --> 00:37:39.650
It must be a bio-computer.

00:37:39.650 --> 00:37:41.320
Bio-computer?

00:37:41.980 --> 00:37:47.450
It's made from bio-chips.
Slimy little blobs of living matter.

00:37:47.450 --> 00:37:50.160
No one in Japan knows
how to make them yet.

00:37:50.160 --> 00:37:52.200
Then this was built...

00:37:52.200 --> 00:37:58.210
Everyone's working on it,
but the only success was at...

00:37:58.670 --> 00:38:00.040
The Pentagon!

00:38:00.540 --> 00:38:03.090
The American military!

00:38:03.960 --> 00:38:05.970
But that means...

00:38:05.970 --> 00:38:09.220
Wait! You kids always
go off half-cocked.

00:38:09.220 --> 00:38:13.470
Know your enemy, know yourself,
and you'll win every battle.

00:38:23.230 --> 00:38:24.030
Mr. Terada!

00:38:24.400 --> 00:38:25.690
You're late!

00:38:25.690 --> 00:38:28.860
I'm sorry.
What about the bed?

00:38:28.860 --> 00:38:32.030
I don't know.
We'll find out when we see it.

00:38:35.750 --> 00:38:39.330
All of you!
Get back to work!

00:38:55.850 --> 00:38:57.100
What's happening?

00:39:05.400 --> 00:39:07.570
We got it to stand up.

00:39:07.940 --> 00:39:11.070
What a fascinating
computer!

00:39:11.070 --> 00:39:13.280
Old age keeps getting better!

00:39:13.280 --> 00:39:15.240
What are you doing now?

00:39:15.240 --> 00:39:19.370
Once a baby stands,
a parent can get it to walk.

00:39:52.280 --> 00:39:55.620
What's happening? Stop it!
Find the switch!

00:39:55.620 --> 00:39:57.040
Impossible!

00:40:14.430 --> 00:40:16.930
What the hell is going on?

00:40:44.710 --> 00:40:46.710
It's that girl!

00:40:46.920 --> 00:40:49.840
She must be controlling it!

00:40:50.460 --> 00:40:51.460
Follow me!

00:40:55.800 --> 00:40:57.640
Mum, look!

00:42:07.120 --> 00:42:08.540
It stopped.

00:42:08.540 --> 00:42:10.380
Haruko!

00:42:10.380 --> 00:42:13.500
What are you
doing over there?

00:42:13.500 --> 00:42:17.220
I have to go!
Take care of things here!

00:42:17.220 --> 00:42:18.550
Haruko!

00:42:18.550 --> 00:42:21.260
Where should we go,
Honey?

00:42:21.970 --> 00:42:24.770
Where should we go,
Honey?

00:42:24.970 --> 00:42:26.060
Did you hear that?

00:42:26.060 --> 00:42:28.560
Someone was talking!

00:42:28.560 --> 00:42:30.940
Where should we go?

00:42:30.940 --> 00:42:32.650
It's the computer!

00:42:34.320 --> 00:42:36.780
The computer has taken
on a personality!

00:42:36.780 --> 00:42:39.530
It's evolving!

00:42:39.530 --> 00:42:41.530
Kamakura.

00:42:48.960 --> 00:42:51.960
This special bulletin
has just come in.

00:42:51.960 --> 00:42:56.760
This morning at 9am,
an unidentified robot...

00:42:58.880 --> 00:43:03.430
An unidentified robot terrorised
shoppers in the Kanto district.

00:43:03.430 --> 00:43:05.520
This sounds like science fiction.

00:43:05.520 --> 00:43:09.350
A reporter is on the scene.
We take you there now.

00:43:09.350 --> 00:43:11.440
Miss Sakata?

00:43:11.440 --> 00:43:13.940
I'm at the scene of
a bizarre crime.

00:43:13.940 --> 00:43:17.990
You can see the destruction
everywhere around me.

00:43:17.990 --> 00:43:23.990
No one knows where this
mysterious robot came from.

00:43:24.200 --> 00:43:26.290
Hey, look at this!

00:43:27.290 --> 00:43:30.920
What? I think
I'm going to puke!

00:43:49.270 --> 00:43:52.100
Damn it! I knew
this was the place!

00:43:52.560 --> 00:43:53.810
Hey, nice system!

00:43:55.690 --> 00:43:59.240
Has anybody seen that girl?

00:43:58.110 --> 00:44:01.150
<i>This is a hospital! Please keep it down!</i>

00:44:03.530 --> 00:44:06.780
Where is she?
Hey, you!

00:44:07.620 --> 00:44:10.080
Yoshio!

00:44:14.580 --> 00:44:17.380
Damn it!
Let's go, Hasegawa!

00:44:18.420 --> 00:44:20.720
This is a hospital!

00:44:20.720 --> 00:44:25.890
Come back to me, Yoshio!

00:44:56.920 --> 00:44:57.840
Here it comes.

00:45:02.800 --> 00:45:05.470
It's added quite
a few parts.

00:45:06.590 --> 00:45:08.810
Begin the operation.

00:45:08.810 --> 00:45:10.260
Move everyone into position.

00:45:19.230 --> 00:45:20.690
Proceed.

00:45:29.700 --> 00:45:32.580
Please minimise
the damage.

00:45:32.580 --> 00:45:36.580
Headquarters has already told us
not to hurt the man inside.

00:45:36.580 --> 00:45:40.040
Actually, I want you to protect
the machine. It's very valuable.

00:45:55.060 --> 00:45:56.980
Just a little further.

00:45:56.980 --> 00:45:59.810
Are the men from
Nishibashi ready?

00:45:59.810 --> 00:46:00.980
Stop!

00:46:00.980 --> 00:46:04.400
No! You'll hurt him!

00:46:02.980 --> 00:46:05.110
<i>It's her! Grab her!</i>

00:46:05.110 --> 00:46:06.280
Arrest her!

00:46:17.080 --> 00:46:18.830
Let go of me!

00:46:18.830 --> 00:46:20.460
Mr. Takazawa!

00:46:20.460 --> 00:46:25.130
What are you doing?
Release that girl at once!

00:46:25.130 --> 00:46:27.220
Who said that?

00:46:43.320 --> 00:46:44.820
Stop the robot!

00:47:25.230 --> 00:47:26.610
Are you all right?

00:47:27.650 --> 00:47:30.110
Yes, I'm fine.
How's Mr. Takazawa?

00:47:30.110 --> 00:47:33.570
He's fine.
He's finally fallen asleep.

00:47:33.950 --> 00:47:35.080
That voice!

00:47:35.700 --> 00:47:38.330
Well, if you'll excuse me...

00:47:50.970 --> 00:47:52.260
After it!

00:47:57.180 --> 00:48:01.440
Let me go!

00:48:01.440 --> 00:48:05.520
You've ruined our project, and
the hope of this nation's elderly!

00:48:05.520 --> 00:48:08.030
I did what I had to do.

00:48:09.150 --> 00:48:11.990
Mr. Terada,
we have to catch it!

00:48:11.990 --> 00:48:14.530
You'll take full
responsibility for this!

00:48:14.530 --> 00:48:16.530
Haruko!

00:48:22.370 --> 00:48:23.330
Get him!

00:48:30.920 --> 00:48:32.510
Got you!

00:48:32.510 --> 00:48:34.010
Maeda!

00:48:34.890 --> 00:48:37.050
Haruko!

00:48:37.050 --> 00:48:39.270
Hang in there, Maeda!

00:48:41.430 --> 00:48:42.850
Wait!

00:48:49.320 --> 00:48:50.280
Where's it heading?

00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:51.650
Towards Kanagawa.

00:48:51.650 --> 00:48:53.950
Could you scoot over?

00:48:53.950 --> 00:48:56.160
Oh, sure.
Hasegawa, move over.

00:48:57.240 --> 00:48:58.450
It's you!

00:48:58.450 --> 00:49:02.290
What are you doing here?
Get out!

00:49:09.710 --> 00:49:12.300
Send us a news helicopter!

00:49:12.300 --> 00:49:13.340
Call H.Q.!

00:49:13.590 --> 00:49:15.430
I want a shot of this!

00:49:15.430 --> 00:49:16.890
Pardon me.

00:49:18.890 --> 00:49:21.720
That robot is a personal friend.

00:49:24.810 --> 00:49:30.480
You've got some nerve!
Conceited little college co-ed!

00:49:30.480 --> 00:49:33.940
No one can stop
the Z-001 now!

00:49:33.940 --> 00:49:35.780
It's grown too powerful!

00:49:36.450 --> 00:49:38.660
You knew this would happen,
didn't you?

00:49:39.330 --> 00:49:43.160
I never expected such a
radical transformation.

00:49:43.160 --> 00:49:45.330
This is beyond
everyone's expectations!

00:49:45.580 --> 00:49:49.040
You were just
using the Ministry!

00:49:49.040 --> 00:49:50.880
Secretary Minagawa has
been fully informed.

00:49:52.000 --> 00:49:52.920
Damn!

00:49:52.920 --> 00:49:55.420
So that nursing bed...

00:49:55.420 --> 00:50:00.300
The computer's the problem.
The bed was just a ploy.

00:50:00.510 --> 00:50:02.010
I wasn't lying.

00:50:02.010 --> 00:50:05.690
My company <i>is</i> planning
to sell a nursing bed.

00:50:05.690 --> 00:50:10.360
But it was a perfect test for
our new multi-purpose computer.

00:50:10.360 --> 00:50:12.530
It was a
military project!

00:50:12.530 --> 00:50:17.490
You told me you cared about
the elderly! You lied to me!

00:50:17.490 --> 00:50:20.910
I didn't dare tell you
that it was a weapons test.

00:50:20.910 --> 00:50:23.830
Message from the ground:
They've lost the target!

00:50:24.080 --> 00:50:25.120
What?

00:50:25.120 --> 00:50:26.210
It's all right.

00:50:29.290 --> 00:50:31.340
I know where it's going.

00:50:34.550 --> 00:50:36.840
What's wrong, Nobuko?

00:50:37.430 --> 00:50:38.380
Where's Haruko?

00:50:38.380 --> 00:50:41.300
Help me with the patients.

00:50:41.300 --> 00:50:42.760
Where's Haruko?

00:50:42.760 --> 00:50:43.760
Kamakura!

00:50:43.760 --> 00:50:44.430
Kamakura?

00:50:44.720 --> 00:50:45.980
Kamakura?

00:50:47.560 --> 00:50:50.520
I'm sure that's
where Takazawa wants to go.

00:50:50.520 --> 00:50:55.440
The bed now has a personality
based on Takazawa's memories.

00:50:55.440 --> 00:50:58.200
I'm looking at his
psychological profile right now.

00:50:59.160 --> 00:51:00.660
Mr. Takazawa!

00:51:04.290 --> 00:51:07.080
What's it doing up there?

00:51:07.080 --> 00:51:09.000
How did it manage that?

00:51:09.000 --> 00:51:11.420
After it! Hurry!

00:51:18.130 --> 00:51:22.050
It's using the monorail track!

00:51:28.520 --> 00:51:30.980
Mr. Takazawa!

00:51:45.410 --> 00:51:48.200
Stop!
This is very dangerous!

00:51:48.450 --> 00:51:50.160
Get down from there!

00:51:50.160 --> 00:51:51.960
Take us closer!

00:51:52.880 --> 00:51:56.250
I said
this is too dangerous!

00:51:56.250 --> 00:51:59.050
Pull over now!

00:51:59.050 --> 00:52:00.340
Mr. Takazawa!

00:52:03.930 --> 00:52:06.220
Mr. Takazawa!

00:52:06.220 --> 00:52:08.720
You idiot!
You'll get yourself killed!

00:52:09.060 --> 00:52:10.850
Let me go!

00:52:10.850 --> 00:52:13.060
You pervert!

00:52:13.060 --> 00:52:13.650
Be quiet!

00:52:13.650 --> 00:52:16.270
No, just leave it
in the container.

00:52:16.270 --> 00:52:19.400
I want you to bring it. The
Secretary has given permission.

00:52:24.950 --> 00:52:25.950
Mr. Terada!

00:52:33.750 --> 00:52:37.380
Let me down!

00:52:39.920 --> 00:52:42.170
We can't keep flying this low.

00:52:42.170 --> 00:52:43.340
Then fly on ahead.

00:52:43.340 --> 00:52:44.720
What about Mr. Terada?

00:52:45.850 --> 00:52:48.720
Wait!

00:52:58.940 --> 00:53:00.900
This is too dangerous!

00:53:00.900 --> 00:53:04.320
Relax, Mr. Terada. Your
blood pressure is rising.

00:53:04.320 --> 00:53:05.990
Who said that?
The old man?

00:53:06.240 --> 00:53:10.740
Your blood pressure is up to 197.
Your pulse rate is 103.

00:53:10.740 --> 00:53:13.710
Too much excitement
could strain your heart.

00:53:15.420 --> 00:53:18.000
Who are you?
The computer?

00:53:18.340 --> 00:53:21.590
I'm Takazawa's wife, Haru.

00:53:21.590 --> 00:53:22.550
What?

00:53:25.970 --> 00:53:27.260
Are you all right?

00:53:27.260 --> 00:53:29.850
Let me go,
you overgrown calculator!

00:53:29.850 --> 00:53:32.430
Take me back to
the Ministry!

00:53:32.430 --> 00:53:36.400
You're the people who put
my husband in such pain.

00:53:36.400 --> 00:53:39.860
Try to understand
how we elderly feel!

00:53:39.860 --> 00:53:43.110
But this project was
intended to help the elderly!

00:53:43.110 --> 00:53:45.280
And now you've ruined it!

00:53:44.030 --> 00:53:45.280
<i>Enough!</i>

00:53:46.530 --> 00:53:50.160
A nurse is useless
unless she can love her patient.

00:53:50.160 --> 00:53:52.040
But...

00:53:52.040 --> 00:53:55.460
My husband just wants
to go to the beach.

00:53:55.460 --> 00:53:57.040
So sit back and be quiet!

00:53:58.540 --> 00:54:01.170
But there's a news blackout!

00:54:01.170 --> 00:54:04.550
I don't care!
Just keep filming!

00:54:04.550 --> 00:54:07.050
Going where?

00:54:07.050 --> 00:54:09.430
Yui beach?
In Kamakura?

00:54:10.050 --> 00:54:14.640
Some of our patients have a
computer link to the bed.

00:54:14.640 --> 00:54:17.020
You owe me now!

00:54:25.690 --> 00:54:29.320
Haru, I sympathise with
what you're saying...

00:54:29.320 --> 00:54:32.160
but won't you
please turn back?

00:54:33.660 --> 00:54:39.670
This project has its faults,
but it will benefit the elderly.

00:54:41.420 --> 00:54:46.920
Please turn back for their sake.
Please!

00:54:46.920 --> 00:54:48.840
Haru.

00:54:48.840 --> 00:54:52.430
Will you let my husband
see the beach first?

00:54:52.430 --> 00:54:54.770
Will you come back
afterwards?

00:54:54.770 --> 00:54:56.430
I promise.

00:54:56.430 --> 00:54:59.940
You will?
Thank you!

00:55:12.870 --> 00:55:14.370
It's coming!

00:55:14.370 --> 00:55:16.580
Bring the truck around
to the front.

00:55:16.580 --> 00:55:18.580
Bring the truck around!

00:55:27.590 --> 00:55:28.800
There it is!

00:55:33.140 --> 00:55:34.680
Hold on a minute.

00:55:37.640 --> 00:55:39.850
Mr. Terada, you're alive!

00:55:39.850 --> 00:55:41.480
Take down the barricade!

00:55:42.060 --> 00:55:46.150
This bed is going
to Yui Beach!

00:55:46.440 --> 00:55:48.280
What are you
talking about?

00:55:48.280 --> 00:55:50.780
I made a promise
to the computer.

00:55:50.780 --> 00:55:54.030
After we visit the beach,
she'll come back. Hurry up!

00:55:56.990 --> 00:55:59.330
Move back, everyone.
Open the road.

00:56:01.710 --> 00:56:03.330
Bring out the Alpha.

00:56:12.340 --> 00:56:15.100
Hasegawa, what is this?

00:56:15.350 --> 00:56:19.180
This is a combat
version of the Z-001.

00:56:19.180 --> 00:56:23.600
It has no prior programming,
so it will follow our orders.

00:56:23.850 --> 00:56:25.980
Damn you!
What are you doing?

00:56:26.860 --> 00:56:28.230
We're going to crush it.

00:56:28.230 --> 00:56:29.610
What?

00:56:29.610 --> 00:56:33.910
How can you make a promise
to a defective computer?

00:56:35.240 --> 00:56:39.120
Besides, we can't ignore
the destruction it's causing.

00:56:43.120 --> 00:56:45.380
Would you please move aside?

00:56:45.380 --> 00:56:47.920
No, Mr. Takazawa!
Stay back!

00:56:51.170 --> 00:56:53.510
Stop!
Mr. Takazawa's in there!

00:56:55.140 --> 00:56:57.510
Mr. Takazawa, get away!

00:57:06.520 --> 00:57:08.190
Go, bed!

00:57:08.190 --> 00:57:10.730
No one messes with the
Ministry of Public Welfare!

00:57:14.490 --> 00:57:15.200
Idiots.

00:57:15.200 --> 00:57:20.620
The Alpha has the same
computer in a combat frame.

00:57:30.750 --> 00:57:32.380
Mr. Takazawa!

00:57:32.380 --> 00:57:34.420
I told you I'd fix it!

00:57:34.420 --> 00:57:37.470
That cord goes over here!

00:57:47.690 --> 00:57:51.230
Can you hear me, miss?
Why aren't you at the beach yet?

00:57:51.690 --> 00:57:53.990
She looks like she's in trouble.

00:57:54.320 --> 00:57:56.450
The robot!
Mr. Takazawa!

00:57:56.780 --> 00:57:59.160
Looks like
she found her friend.

00:57:59.160 --> 00:58:03.250
Haruko,
Maeda is on his way!

00:58:08.670 --> 00:58:10.290
Haruko!

00:58:11.920 --> 00:58:14.260
I thought we ordered
a news blackout.

00:58:15.050 --> 00:58:18.220
Hurry up and crush
that pile of junk!

00:58:49.460 --> 00:58:51.040
Don't go!
It's too dangerous!

00:58:54.840 --> 00:58:57.760
Doesn't human life
mean anything to you?

00:58:58.010 --> 00:59:00.390
Control that monster of yours!

00:59:00.390 --> 00:59:03.720
You're getting old yourself.
You'll be ready for a bed soon.

00:59:03.720 --> 00:59:06.230
Just stand back
and let me work.

00:59:18.530 --> 00:59:20.410
Haru!

00:59:20.410 --> 00:59:23.780
The beach is on the
other side of this tunnel.

00:59:29.290 --> 00:59:31.420
Almost there.

00:59:47.980 --> 00:59:50.190
It's falling apart!
Get back!

00:59:50.190 --> 00:59:52.980
But Mr. Takazawa's
in there!

01:00:21.630 --> 01:00:24.390
Haru, I'm hungry.

01:00:24.390 --> 01:00:27.970
I have my hands full right now.
Please wait a moment, Darling.

01:00:36.520 --> 01:00:37.980
What happened?

01:00:37.980 --> 01:00:40.740
It's a disaster!
We've lost our link to the Alpha!

01:00:40.740 --> 01:00:42.110
What?!

01:01:36.540 --> 01:01:39.800
What happened to Haruko?

01:01:39.800 --> 01:01:41.300
Do something!

01:01:41.510 --> 01:01:45.300
You don't know what you're asking!
There's a war in there!

01:01:46.090 --> 01:01:48.600
I'll be killed if I go in!

01:01:49.720 --> 01:01:53.770
Seriously, what a wimp!
Be a man!

01:01:55.480 --> 01:01:57.980
Hey, Mister White Knight!

01:01:58.310 --> 01:02:00.940
You know,
a woman loves to be rescued.

01:02:15.580 --> 01:02:17.330
Haruko?

01:02:17.330 --> 01:02:20.590
Please take care
of my husband.

01:02:29.930 --> 01:02:31.390
Mr. Takazawa...

01:02:35.230 --> 01:02:38.440
My wife...

01:02:47.780 --> 01:02:49.700
Mrs. Takazawa!

01:02:49.990 --> 01:02:52.700
Haruko!

01:02:53.030 --> 01:02:55.080
We have to get
out of here!

01:02:55.080 --> 01:02:55.950
No!

01:02:59.790 --> 01:03:01.080
Haruko!
I'm here to rescue you!

01:03:01.540 --> 01:03:03.960
Follow that robot!

01:03:05.050 --> 01:03:09.220
The beach is so close!
We have to catch up to her!

01:03:48.170 --> 01:03:49.470
Mrs. Takazawa!

01:03:59.890 --> 01:04:01.190
Damn!

01:04:07.820 --> 01:04:09.400
Mrs. Takazawa!

01:04:09.400 --> 01:04:10.570
Mummy!

01:04:10.860 --> 01:04:12.660
I'm hungry!

01:04:12.910 --> 01:04:14.530
We have to get out!

01:04:18.870 --> 01:04:23.710
The picture!
What's happening to Haruko?

01:04:23.000 --> 01:04:23.710
<i>Quiet!</i>

01:04:24.170 --> 01:04:25.840
Got it!

01:04:25.840 --> 01:04:26.750
Are you on-line?

01:04:30.260 --> 01:04:32.840
Stop! Stop!

01:04:36.010 --> 01:04:39.560
Can you hear me?
Smash the core chip!

01:04:39.560 --> 01:04:41.310
The only way to kill it...

01:04:41.560 --> 01:04:42.850
is to break its head!

01:04:42.850 --> 01:04:44.900
Where is it?

01:04:44.900 --> 01:04:47.400
It keeps shifting!

01:04:51.820 --> 01:04:54.950
It's in the left rear right now.
We'll direct you!

01:04:55.280 --> 01:04:56.490
Hurry!

01:04:56.490 --> 01:04:59.950
But how can I break it?

01:04:59.950 --> 01:05:02.790
Use this! Hurry!

01:05:03.830 --> 01:05:05.290
An oxygen tank?

01:05:05.540 --> 01:05:07.540
Maeda, give me a hand!

01:05:10.380 --> 01:05:12.550
Hurry! Go!

01:05:15.840 --> 01:05:17.180
What's happening?

01:05:24.690 --> 01:05:27.520
It's out of control!
Let's get out of here!

01:05:47.500 --> 01:05:49.880
What do you think
you're doing?

01:05:50.750 --> 01:05:52.050
Stop!

01:06:02.470 --> 01:06:03.810
Stop!

01:06:27.670 --> 01:06:30.000
Where's the core chip?

01:06:30.290 --> 01:06:31.460
Where is it?

01:06:31.460 --> 01:06:34.050
It's on the upper left side.
Can you see it?

01:06:34.880 --> 01:06:36.880
That fool!

01:06:36.880 --> 01:06:38.430
You idiot!

01:06:38.890 --> 01:06:41.890
Honey, I'll get
you to the beach.

01:06:43.970 --> 01:06:46.690
Haru...

01:06:46.690 --> 01:06:49.440
No one messes with the
Ministry of Public Welfare!

01:06:55.190 --> 01:06:56.990
No!

01:06:56.990 --> 01:06:58.530
Don't!

01:07:09.460 --> 01:07:13.170
Don't do it! Don't do it!

01:07:13.170 --> 01:07:15.420
We're going to the beach!

01:07:25.350 --> 01:07:27.560
Mrs. Takazawa, help!

01:08:29.580 --> 01:08:31.370
I'm hungry!

01:08:35.630 --> 01:08:38.880
Wow, what a show!

01:08:55.520 --> 01:08:57.980
It's still collapsing!

01:09:01.360 --> 01:09:02.950
Mrs. Takazawa!

01:09:16.170 --> 01:09:18.290
Mrs. Takazawa!

01:09:18.290 --> 01:09:20.460
Mrs. Takazawa. Mrs. Takazawa...

01:09:20.460 --> 01:09:21.710
Mrs. Takazawa.

01:09:21.920 --> 01:09:25.800
Haruko, where's my husband?

01:09:25.800 --> 01:09:29.560
Haru!

01:09:32.810 --> 01:09:36.770
Honey, I can't go on.

01:09:38.940 --> 01:09:43.740
Haru!

01:09:44.610 --> 01:09:52.450
But we'll be
together again soon.

01:09:54.040 --> 01:09:55.500
Haru...

01:09:57.210 --> 01:09:58.590
Mr. Takazawa!

01:09:59.130 --> 01:10:02.510
Yes, we'll be
together again soon...

01:10:03.130 --> 01:10:08.260
Hold on, Mr. Takazawa!

01:10:09.640 --> 01:10:12.390
He's a little weak,
but he's fine.

01:10:12.390 --> 01:10:14.020
He'll be okay.

01:10:14.770 --> 01:10:16.270
Mr. Takazawa!

01:10:39.670 --> 01:10:44.800
The damage was caused by the
Ministry of Public Welfare...

01:10:44.800 --> 01:10:48.220
during testing of a new
geriatric-care ambulance.

01:10:48.220 --> 01:10:53.180
Yoshihiko Hasegawa has been
arrested following the accident.

01:10:53.180 --> 01:10:57.730
Hasegawa is a developer at
the Nishibashi Corporation.

01:10:57.730 --> 01:11:03.650
Hasegawa is charged with
delivering a defective computer...

01:11:03.650 --> 01:11:07.860
which was used on board
the runaway ambulance.

01:11:07.860 --> 01:11:13.660
Nishibashi shipments have been
halted pending investigation.

01:11:14.120 --> 01:11:17.660
That sure stirred them up!

01:11:17.870 --> 01:11:22.670
Good work, men,
but our job is done.

01:11:22.670 --> 01:11:27.090
Those lying weasels
covered it up pretty well.

01:11:28.090 --> 01:11:30.760
"The Bad Sleep Well."

01:11:39.310 --> 01:11:40.690
Mr. Terada!

01:11:41.440 --> 01:11:43.650
Could you answer
a question?

01:11:43.650 --> 01:11:46.150
We'd like a statement!

01:11:46.150 --> 01:11:49.320
Secretary Minagawa will
answer all questions.

01:11:49.320 --> 01:11:52.660
As I said in yesterday's
press conference...

01:11:53.950 --> 01:11:56.870
Was there an old man
inside the ambulance?

01:11:56.870 --> 01:11:58.200
Say something!

01:11:58.200 --> 01:12:04.170
Was the old man a guinea pig
in a military weapons test?

01:12:04.750 --> 01:12:08.670
An anonymous source has
provided some interesting files.

01:12:08.670 --> 01:12:09.630
Is this true?

01:12:09.630 --> 01:12:13.300
How could an ambulance
cause so much damage?

01:12:13.300 --> 01:12:14.720
What's <i>really</i> going on?

01:12:15.050 --> 01:12:19.430
I'm sure everything will be
made clear in court.

01:12:19.430 --> 01:12:23.770
However, this project is still
intended to benefit the public.

01:12:23.770 --> 01:12:28.360
Although our first attempt
had problems, we'll fix them.

01:12:28.360 --> 01:12:33.820
I regret that our announcement
made such rumours possible.

01:12:33.820 --> 01:12:34.490
That's all I have to say.

01:12:34.490 --> 01:12:37.370
One moment, Mr. Terada!

01:12:48.590 --> 01:12:51.550
Let's go and see him.

01:12:51.550 --> 01:12:52.680
Sure...

01:13:05.650 --> 01:13:07.320
Are you awake,
Mr. Takazawa?

01:13:08.320 --> 01:13:11.860
I'm just bringing flowers today.
I'll be back soon.

01:13:11.860 --> 01:13:14.780
Go to the beach...

01:13:14.780 --> 01:13:17.120
You sure did
go to the beach!

01:13:17.830 --> 01:13:20.750
You often took
your wife there.

01:13:20.750 --> 01:13:24.500
She'll be coming
for me soon.

01:13:24.500 --> 01:13:27.130
Don't say things
like that.

01:13:27.130 --> 01:13:29.630
You have to think
about getting better.

01:13:29.630 --> 01:13:33.880
Once you're better,
we'll go back to the beach.

01:13:33.880 --> 01:13:37.220
I'm going to the beach.

01:13:37.640 --> 01:13:39.930
Yes, so you...

01:13:40.850 --> 01:13:42.230
An earthquake?

01:13:58.120 --> 01:14:00.370
She came for me.

01:14:07.960 --> 01:14:10.210
I've come for you.

01:14:18.930 --> 01:14:21.560
Haru!

01:14:21.560 --> 01:14:28.810
It took me a while to
get used to this new body.

01:14:28.810 --> 01:14:34.650
So, shall we go to
the beach, Honey?
